Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayGraphics3D", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"f912925e-0bbe-6a4e-9d04-f715c26f0e16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1b81c81f-9317-f248-94ad-9bfe325b797a"],
 " ",
 "draws the array arr as cubes arranged in space."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"a5f123ea-5419-534b-a79e-bec8acb249b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr", ",", " ", "opts"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2d9f607b-6bfe-f94d-831b-1e07a63e8363"],
 " ",
 "draws it with the given options."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"a9c7128e-2033-974e-a210-23145ad74aa1"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"7277ff2b-c31d-6148-89e1-89d8211e102f"],

Cell["\<\
An array of order one is drawn as a line of cubes, one of order two as a \
plane of them, and one of order three as a lattice. The entry at index tuple \
(i, j, k) sits at the point {i, j, k}, an index the array does not have \
standing at one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ed54192-e0c0-4a46-a055-ba0c46f9fa1c"],

Cell["\<\
An array of higher order is drawn by tiling: the inner block of indices is \
drawn as a lattice, and the outer block repeats that lattice through space, \
shifted by its own extent and a gap. Everything ends up in one picture, since \
space has no room for pictures inset into pictures.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d62ccc29-4624-0e47-bcf8-d1c017c8e6f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is always a three-dimensional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Graphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "eb2dae3d-635c-5b4b-8d71-79338a9e52a0"],
 ". For plane pictures at every order see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2b08e242-e1ac-9342-a832-b0b8cd08d456"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"70d599d6-b495-f84d-bfaf-cd38032c1016"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Nesting\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"k1", ",", " ", "k2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"701478f6-749b-5148-9476-da838c04a48f"],
 " says how to split the indices: the blocks must sum to the order of the \
array and each must be one, two or three, space holding no more at a time. \
The default uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayNesting", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"256c97a4-e2e1-8f41-831d-1036ade3f105"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"023a41fc-5393-6447-9ff8-b60a49dff1c7"],

Cell["\<\
The cubes have translucent faces and no outline, so that the entries behind \
them can still be read; an outline on every cube of a lattice reads as a mesh \
rather than as a set of cells.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"59f3f22d-ba37-8446-93b8-837fa6646457"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A gnomon in the near corner marks as many axes as the picture uses; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Gnomon\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"881a0fd0-abf0-f94d-a4c4-d35156585e80"],
 " drops it. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Indices\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Colored\>\""}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0c14b069-e6b5-ee44-aff8-b6b2609b6061"],
 " gives each axis a colour of its own."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ee44e3e9-2d8e-0e48-b265-f5404ea31773"],

Cell["\<\
The reference implementation this package grew out of drew only the \
order-three case, and called such a picture a cubix; the name is not kept, \
but the look of it is.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"277946cb-8ba0-0149-b5ec-5c64145911d5"],

Cell["The other options are shared with ArrayGraphics.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"db29abc3-7d3f-1e49-bff8-0fd33647c05a"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"dfda8956-06f9-6948-964a-6b154810c531"],

Cell["At order one a line of cubes, at order two a plane of them:", \
"ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"e894e325-eb29-1c41-b151-7853f2f7c780"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics3D[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics3D[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4e9111e0-202a-be42-86ac-d76c53e1a2ba"],

